  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 112 PM CDT Sat Jul 25 2026\n\nTonight through next Friday...Through much of this forecast period, \nstrong high pressure aloft remains wedged into the region from the \nwest, while high pressure at the surface remains wedged in from the \nsouth.  While the stalled surface boundary to the north of the CWA \nwill washout through the weekend, an isolated shower or storm will \nremain possible across the area each afternoon through mid-week in \nthis moist and unstable airmass.\n\nAt the end of the forecast period, next Thursday into Friday, the \naforementioned high aloft will weaken its presence across eastern \nportion of the region.  This will allow troughing along the east \ncoast to deepen across the Southeast United States.  As this \nhappens, another surface boundary will attempt to sink south into \nthe CWA.  Thus, increasing rain chances across the area and possibly \nbringing at least some temporary relief to the main weather focus of \nthis forecast period...the oppressive heat.\n\nBeginning Sunday and continuing through at least mid-week, high \nlevels of both heat and humidity will yield a lengthy period of \ndangerous heat stress across the forecast area.  While high \ntemperatures Sunday will generally hover in the mid and upper 90s, \nthey'll range more in the upper 90s on Monday, and upper 90s to just \nabove 100 Tuesday into Wednesday.  These temperatures, in addition to \ndew points in the 70s, will result in afternoon heat index values at \nand above 106 across the CWA, again beginning Sunday.\n\nAs a result, a \"Heat Advisory\" has now been hoisted across the \nforecast area on Sunday from 11 AM - 9 PM as indices range between \n106-110 for at least a couple of hours.  The exception to this is \nacross Bolivar, Sunflower, & Leflore counties where afternoon heat \nindex values will climb above 110 for an hour or two.  Here, an \n\"Extreme Heat Warning\" has been issued for Sunday from 11 AM until \n9 PM.\n\nAs this dangerous heat stress increases Monday through mid-week, a \ncontinuation of the \"Heat Advisory\" into the work week is expected, \nwith further expansion of the \"Extreme Heat Warning\" across the CWA \nlikely.  This will be messaged in the latest HWO graphic. However at \nthe moment, an assessment of the layout and continuation of heat-\nrelated products will be made on a daily basis.  Therefore, please \ncontinue to monitor the latest forecast for the most up-to-date \ninformation. /19/",
